Root cause
----------

The crashing image has malformed group local-quota info:

  type =3D 1
  dqi_flags =3D 0x20001
  dqi_chunks =3D 0
  dqi_blocks =3D 2

The on-disk local quota info is trusted by ocfs2_local_read_info().
Since dqi_chunks is zero, ocfs2_load_local_quota_bitmaps() loads an
empty chunk list.
Later, when creat(2) needs a group dquot,
ocfs2_local_quota_add_chunk() extends the local quota file and appends
the first in-memory chunk.

However, ocfs2_local_quota_add_chunk() computes the new chunk number
from the previous list entry after list_add_tail():

  chunk->qc_num =3D list_entry(chunk->qc_chunk.prev,
                             struct ocfs2_quota_chunk, qc_chunk)->qc_num + =
1;

If the list was empty, chunk->qc_chunk.prev is the list head embedded
in struct ocfs2_mem_dqinfo, not a struct ocfs2_quota_chunk. The code
therefore reads qc_num from unrelated fields after the list head.

GDB captured the following values on the reproducer:

  [GDB add_chunk] type=3D1 oinfo=3D0xff110000313c3800 chunks=3D1 blocks=3D4
  list_head=3D0xff110000313c3818 prev=3D0xff110000313c3818
  chunk=3D0xff1100002e6d9ae0 qc_num=3D778813537
  gqinode=3D0xff1100002e6bc060

  [GDB create_ldq] type=3D1 chunk=3D0xff1100002e6d9ae0 qc_num=3D778813537
dq_local_off=3D3373318656

  [GDB release] dq_type=3D1 od=3D0xff1100002e6dd400 chunk=3D0xff1100002e6d9=
ae0
  qc_num=3D778813537 dq_local_off=3D3373318656 offset=3D-1241513984
  headerbh=3D0xff1100002e6d6bc8 b_data=3D0xff11000012e46400
dchunk=3D0xff11000012e46400

That bogus qc_num makes ocfs2_local_release_dquot() compute a bogus
bitmap offset, and the bit clear writes far outside the local quota
bitmap.

Fix
---

The proposed patch does two things:

  1. Validate local quota info before loading/recovering the bitmap state:
     reject unknown dqi_flags bits, dqi_blocks outside the local quota file=
,
     impossible zero-chunk geometry, too many chunks, and inconsistent
     dqi_chunks/dqi_blocks geometry.

  2. In ocfs2_local_quota_add_chunk(), derive the new chunk number from the
     current dqi_chunks value saved before incrementing the on-disk count,
     instead of deriving it from the previous list entry. This also makes t=
he
     empty-list case correct.

I built a patched kernel from a clean source and ran the same compiled
C reproducer. The image was rejected during quota initialization, with
no KASAN report and no panic.

If you have any questions, please let me know.

